{"name":"China Blue","hex":"#5a6c80","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"china blue","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pale blue-grey colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale blue-grey colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/china_blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"China Blue","blocks":[{"text":"China Blue is a 2005 documentary film directed by Micha Peled. It follows the life of Jasmine Li, a seventeen-year-old worker from Sichuan, in a Chinese jeans factory, Lifeng Clothes Factory (丽锋服饰制衣有限公司) in Shaxi, Guangdong producing Vigaze Jeans, hence the title. Jasmine earned about half a yuan for one hour's work."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/99/China_Blue_FilmPoster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_Blue"},{"title":"China Blue (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"China Blue\" is a song by German pop singer Fancy. It was released as a single in December 1987 and subsequently included on his 1988 album Flames of Love."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_Blue_(song)"},{"title":"China","blocks":[{"text":"China, officially the People's Republic of China (PRC), is a country in East Asia. It is divided into 33 province-level divisions, including two special administrative regions. Beijing is the capital, while Shanghai is the most populous city by urban area. Its geography features the Central Plain, major rivers such as the Yangtze and Yellow River, deserts, subtropical and temperate forests, plateaus, and mountain ranges such as the Himalayas. It is the world's second-most populous country after India, with a population exceeding 1.4 billion. Covering 9.6 million square kilometers (3,700,000 sq mi), it is the third largest country by area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/MET_DP219959.jpg/500px-MET_DP219959.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/MET_DP219959.jpg/1280px-MET_DP219959.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/MET_DP219959.jpg/500px-MET_DP219959.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A set of Western Zhou-era ritual bronzes, c. 1000 BCE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMET_DP219959.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Terracotta_Army_%286143564816%29.jpg/500px-Terracotta_Army_%286143564816%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Terracotta_Army_%286143564816%29.jpg